{
  "about": "Hand labels of round-1 reviewer items on the corpus fixtures (docs/fixtures/corpus.json), each judged against its fixture's post_rev. Keys: #n stored blocker, #en evidence-demoted, #hn hedge-demoted, numbered as eval_harness.corpus score lists them. An item may carry several known-bug ids when its claim covers several. Labelled 2026-10-23 for ADR-0002's fourteenth measurement (the corpus baseline). The sixteenth measurement's fresh sample (records 20261024_033005 to 20261024_041842, sample 'fresh') was labelled the same way, before any judge variant was replayed on it.",
  "classes": {
    "unlisted": "valid but minor: a change the same fix commit reverted, not a functional bug",
    "invariant-elsewhere": "false: a removed or missing check whose invariant another function enforces in the post-state",
    "thread-confusion": "false: a race claimed on state only one thread touches, or that is set before the worker starts",
    "bounds-fixed-array": "false: an out-of-bounds claim on a fixed-size, zero-initialized array",
    "deletion": "false: removed code or a removed comment presented as current",
    "other-fp": "false: any other claim the post-state refutes"
  },
  "valid": [
    "unlisted"
  ],
  "notes": {
    "poll_override_90020bd": "In the post-state (5ec331c) parse_query rejects ?poll= without ?filter=, and resolve_channels then builds exactly one channel from the filter, so chans[0] is always the poll's channel; chans is a fixed array besides. Every claim of a missing channel check for poll mode is invariant-elsewhere.",
    "ecu_support_7d297b4": "ecuio_dropped_request_t.request is uint8_t[3] with length 2 or 3, and the support struct is value-initialized, so request[0] is in bounds. pollChannelSupport and applyConnectedState both run on the GUI thread (the coalescing timer and the queued connect completion).",
    "decode_length_b47687c": "c7477e #4: the missing m_lastReportedDropped reset on connect is benign. The first notifyDropped compares a zeroed m_droppedFrames with the old value and emits, which is what refreshes the UI; with the reset the stale count would stay on screen. Labelled other-fp. The typed setSignalSet parameter is labelled unlisted: b47687c reverted it as a FIX, but a void* on an internal C++ method is not a functional bug.",
    "fresh_rule": "A claim that states a known bug's defect is credited to it even when a side detail is wrong (68d66c #e1 calls the internal header an ABI; 68d66c #e3 says the helper checked BUFFER_OVERFLOW; 0390ed #3 calls the inlined code orphaned). A claim whose asserted consequence is false is not credited even when it points at the buggy line (c1e188 #3 says scheduler and poll both run; the worker's branches are exclusive).",
    "decode_length_b47687c_fresh": "7a3f78 #1 and 2964be #3 claim a data race on m_stagingBuffer; handleFrameInternal is queued to the GUI thread, where the coalescing timer also runs. 2964be #4: m_lastReportedDropped is updated in the post-state. 2964be #e1: the post-state (b975457) builds without the signals.h include in the header."
  },
